  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthened institutional capacity of employers&apos; organizations</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The two Employer and Business Membership Organizations (EBMOs) in Bosnia and Herzegovina operate in a complex and challenging business environment, further complicated by the country&#x2019;s fragmented administrative structure. Their member enterprises are increasingly seeking support to navigate frequent legislative changes - driven in part by EU accession commitments - and to adapt to regional and global trends. Weak social dialogue further hinders meaningful engagement with policymakers and limits efforts to shape a more enabling business environment. To meet these challenges and growing expectations, the EBMOs must strengthen their organizational capacity to deliver relevant services and effectively represent business interests.
ILO interventions in 2024-2025 focus on two main areas. First, the ILO continues to support the EBMOs in enhancing their service portfolios. This builds on earlier progress - the ILO has supported the Association of Employers of the Federation of Bosnia and Herzegovina (UPFBiH) in launching an OSH training service, and assisted the Union of Employers of Republika Srpska (UERS) in developing a service to help companies digitalize operations and improve their online presence. While both services have been well received, further support is needed to ensure their sustainability. The focus is on scaling up training and reviewing sustainability plans, paying particular attention to the UPFBiH.
The second intervention aims to support improved EBMO performance by expanding membership and streamlining internal operations. An in-depth institutional and capacity assessment will be conducted to gauge member satisfaction, identify needs, and inform the development of future strategic plans. Support focuses on implementing key measures, including optimized membership management and improved internal processes.</narrative>
  </description>
